import{_ as r,o as a,c as t,a5 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Plan","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/trend-graph-core/plan.md","filePath":"feature/trend-graph-core/plan.md"}'),i={name:"feature/trend-graph-core/plan.md"};function n(s,e,l,d,c,p){return a(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="plan" tabindex="-1">Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Plan&quot;">​</a></h1><ol><li>AI models define bounded search/neighborhood and explicit node/edge/result contracts. New graph explorer service uses parameterized Cypher, read sessions, one managed transaction per request, transaction timeout and overall deadline.</li><li>Search pages include limit+1 lookahead; neighborhood uses bounded breadth-first expansion (fanout+1 per node), deterministic ordering, elementId deduplication, endpoint closure, property allowlists and truncation reasons. No path explosion or APOC dependency. Both endpoints restrict public trend graph vocabulary.</li><li>Protected explorer router is mounted before the legacy catch-all trend route. Fix legacy real-driver traversal to rethrow failures and select the real root even if it has no relationships; retain its successful response contract.</li><li>Business thin controller, request records and Admin service guard every method before forwarding. Validate bounded input and upstream shape. Map only graph resource-not-found to 404. Add an explicit encoded-URI GET method to the shared client to prevent WebClient double encoding; existing String calls keep their behavior. Verify raw query strings with a local HTTP stub. Node search and expansion share public-node predicates and parameter bounds; explicit label validation avoids dynamic label/Cypher injection.</li><li>Local-only unit/HTTP fixtures and direct read-only live graph smoke validate no writes, real topology, empty vs missing vs unavailable, and authorization. No frontend or locale changes in this backend-only phase.</li></ol><h2 id="operational-notes" tabindex="-1">Operational notes <a class="header-anchor" href="#operational-notes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Operational notes&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Existing pipeline/Neo4j credentials remain server-side; READ_ACCESS selects the read routing mode, not a database permission boundary. Only fixed read Cypher is exposed. A dedicated read-only Neo4j account can be provisioned separately; this phase does not rotate or reduce the writer&#39;s existing credentials.</li><li>Uses the importing-WITH subquery form supported before Neo4j 5.23. Current Aura emits a deprecation warning for that form; queries succeed. No APOC, graph DDL or installation of Bloom is required for these APIs.</li><li>Start/restart Business and AI to register the routes after review. No automatic service restart is performed during implementation. JWT/Gateway live smoke is separate from isolated controller and direct Neo4j checks.</li><li>Driver reference: <a href="https://neo4j.com/docs/api/python-driver/current/api.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://neo4j.com/docs/api/python-driver/current/api.html</a></li></ul>',4)])])}const m=r(i,[["render",n]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
